# Optional. Everything has a safe default; the lab needs no tenant and no credentials (it holds none), and Mock needs no network.
# The shared settings file is ~/Development/.env (mode 600; STANDALONE_ENV overrides the path), read by every standalone app.
# There is no per-app .env file. This lab reads three optional keys from the shared file:
# ROUTE_LAB_MODE=mock             # the mode the page opens in. mock is the default. live opens in Live only when Live is also on (below)
# ROUTE_LAB_LIVE=1                # opt-in, exactly 1. Lets the Request simulator send one request to the target below. Off when unset
# ROUTE_LAB_LIVE_TARGET=https://localhost:3036   # your local gateway: ONE origin on this machine (localhost, 127.x.x.x, [::1]); no override
# Per-run settings (shell, not the shared file; the shared file holds no PORT):
# PORT=5050                       # must be in 5050-5099
# LAB_BIND=127.0.0.1              # loopback only unless you set this on purpose (the container does). Live is refused on a wider bind outside the container
